# InterMUN UI — seamun.com

Designs should feel calm, crisp, and Apple-like — matching [seamun.com](https://seamun.com).

## Typography
- **UI everywhere** (body, headings, buttons, nav, marketing, auth): system SF stack (`-apple-system` / SF Pro) with Inter fallback
- Hierarchy = size + weight only (`400` body · `600` subheads · `700` titles)
- Letter-spacing slightly tight on titles (`-0.01em` to `-0.02em`)
- **Documents only** (resolutions / papers): Merriweather via `.font-serif`
- Dyslexic mode: OpenDyslexic (with Atkinson Hyperlegible fallback)
- Do **not** mix Instrument Serif, Clash Display, cursive scripts, or Inter Tight into product UI

## Color & Tone (seamun.com tokens)
- Background base: grouped gray `#F2F2F7`
- Elevated surfaces: white `#FFFFFF`
- Ink: `#1D1D1F` · secondary `#6E6E73` · tertiary `#AEAEB2`
- Primary / accent: Apple blue `#007AFF` (hover `#0077ED`)
- Borders / separators: `#D1D1D6` / `rgba(60, 60, 67, 0.29)`
- Soft shadows only: `0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)` — no heavy glow

## Radii & Controls
- Radii: `8 / 10 / 12 / 16 / 20` · pills `980px`
- Primary buttons: Apple-blue filled pills, no lift/scale on hover
- Secondary: light fill / hairline border pills

## Layout & Composition
- Auth / gates: dark brand panel (`#1D1D1F`) + white form (desktop)
- White section cards on gray canvas; generous whitespace
- Prefer asymmetry / staggered sections; never clone identical section structures back-to-back

## Constraints
- Keep existing component naming/IA intact
- Enhance via tokens (color, radius, shadow, motion) — do not change labels or structural naming
